          "ext": "pdf",
          "summary": "FirstLight Power presents a revised methodology for winter load shape and weather year selection used in Capacity Accreditation Review (CAR-SA), proposing to optimize weights using 5-day blocks rather than individual days to better capture multi-day cold weather events critical for energy storage accreditation. The revised approach responds to ISO-NE and stakeholder feedback from the May 2026 Markets Committee by targeting the full 70-year historical distribution rather than only the extreme tail. FirstLight argues the ISO's current methodology over-represents extreme multi-day weather events and that correcting this would affect storage resource accreditation outcomes and ultimately consumer costs.",
